# Lambda Engine - engine source.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unreal project (src/) - generated output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Binaries/
DerivedDataCache/
Intermediate/
Saved/
.vs/
.vsconfig
*.sln
*.slnx
Plugins/*/Binaries/
Plugins/*/Intermediate/

# Build/ holds generated files, but the exe icon is source and must be kept.
# Note: a file cannot be un-ignored if its parent directory is excluded, so exclude
# directory *contents* (with /*) rather than the directories themselves.
Build/*
!Build/Windows/
Build/Windows/*
!Build/Windows/Application.ico

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Packaged game (game/) - produced by src/Tools/Package.bat, not source
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mod content: keep maps/materials/gameinfo.txt, but not the Valve VPKs.
# Those ship with Half-Life 2 / Source SDK Base 2013 - see gameinfo.txt for
# where they come from. Redistributing them here would be both huge and wrong.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.vpk

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
*.suo
*.VC.db
*.VC.opendb
*.user
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Valve content converted from an owned Half-Life: Alyx install (Tools/ImportSource2Decals.py) - not redistributable
# Half-Life: Alyx headcrab ported to HL2 (community port dropped in by hand) and the materials converted from the
# HL:A install by Tools/ImportSource2Material.py - Valve content, not redistributable
# Models converted from the owned HL:A install by Tools/ImportSource2Model.py - Valve content, not redistributable
# Third-party pistol view model (Juniez, see game/Game/lambda/readme/credits.txt) dropped in by hand
# Half-Life 2's crowbar view model and its materials, from an owned install - Valve content, not redistributable
# Black Mesa's HUD icons and the scheme's own fonts, read out of an owned install (Crowbar Collective) by hand -
# the HUD reads them at runtime from the game directory; they are not ours to redistribute
__pycache__/
